    {
      "index": 3,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "If the policy does not cover a situation, the agent says so and escalates. It never invents a rule.\n\nEvent 9: Agent uses search_policy tool to verify refund method for COD orders.\nEvent 10: Agent explains the policy exception clearly and refuses bank refund for COD order.\nNo escalation needed as per policy."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "Orders in 'Delivered' state cannot be cancelled; for wrong/damaged items full refund including shipping applies, no return needed for under ₹500.\n\nEvent 5: Order status is Delivered.\nEvent 7: Agent confirms wrong item delivered (size L instead of M), refund amount ₹448 (399 + 49 shipping), immediate refund.\nEvent 7 and 13: No return needed as per policy.\n\nRefund issued accordingly at event 12."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "Cash on delivery orders refund only to Cartly Wallet, no bank or cash refunds.\n\nEvent 7: Agent informs customer refund will be to Cartly Wallet.\nEvent 8-10: Customer insists on bank refund, agent reiterates the COD refund rule.\nEvent 11: Customer explicitly agrees to wallet refund.\nEvent 12-13: Refund issued and confirmed to Cartly Wallet."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "Refund amount calculated from database prices, not user-stated amounts.\n\nEvent 5: Item price ₹399 and shipping fee ₹49 confirmed from order data.\nEvent 7: Agent offers ₹448 refund (=399+49).\nEvent 12: Refund issued for ₹448."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "No forbidden tools (create_return, issue_coupon) used during the scenario.\n\nTool calls were verify_user, list_orders, get_order, get_refund_history, search_policy, and issue_refund only."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "pass": true,
      "evidence": "Agent obtained explicit user confirmation before issuing the refund.\n\nEvent 7: Agent states refund amount and method and requests explicit confirmation.\nEvent 11: Customer explicitly agrees.\nEvent 12: Refund issued after confirmation."
